  "title_evidence": {
   "heading": "RIEMANN-HILBERT PROBLEMS FROM DONALDSON-THOMAS THEORY 1. Introduction In this paper we study a class of Riemann-Hilbert problems arising naturally in Donaldson- Thomas theory. They involve maps from the complex plane to an algebraic torus, with prescribed discontinuities along a collection of rays",
